    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d912">

                <pb facs="0997" n="905" sameAs="frus:frus1918Supp01v01/pg905"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 763.72111/6916a</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                        Minister in Persia</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Caldwell</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1918-03-29T20:00:00-05:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">March 29, 1918, 8 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>34. It is reported in the newspapers that a Persian delegation has left Teheran
                    for Berlin via Constantinople to arrange a permanent alliance between Persia and
                    Germany based upon a large loan by Germany to finance Persian railroads and to
                    equip the Persian Army with German instructors.</p>
                <p>Please investigate and report immediately upon this matter.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Lansing</hi>
                        
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
